<p>NOTE: The firm reported a net loss of $5,637,000 or $0.44 per share for the quarter ended June 30, 1997, following a charge to earnings which totaled $7,901,000 ($5,816,000 after tax or $.45 per share after tax). For the six-month period ended June 30, l997, Multiple Zones reported a net loss of $3,571,000 or $.28 per share, which compares to net income of $4,615,000 or $.45 per share for the six-month period ended June 30, 1996. The Company recorded several charges to second quarter earnings totaling $7.9 million.  The charges include reserves relating to slow moving and excess inventories, uncollectible vendor coop receivables, goodwill in foreign subsidiaries, and other miscellaneous items.  The charge also includes costs associated with recent management changes and internal process reorganizations implemented by CEO, John DeFeo.</p>
